\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{ZY} & =y-z \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,4⟩-⟨-1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{ZX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{ZY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ZX}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{ZY}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ZX}||\\overset{\\to }{ZY}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{40}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{240}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{4\\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{15}})={25}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305589 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305590 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305591 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305592 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305593 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1041 "selection" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1104 #edb/ref 17592186305590 13194139534721 true] [17592186305588 1110 #uuid "45442419-9910-5c12-9801-3473e30f7e7e" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305589 1034 "{23}^{∘}" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305589 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534721 true] [17592186305589 1111 #uuid "b799d246-a11b-5070-8463-6dd43a31f2fe" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305590 1034 "{25}^{∘}" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305590 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534721 true] [17592186305590 1111 #uuid "0efd139f-2138-5c6a-8e89-f0113b4b5529" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305591 1034 "{28}^{∘}" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534721 true] [17592186305591 1111 #uuid "5e90994a-68d7-554e-8846-e8e826dcaf09" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305592 1034 "{30}^{∘}" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305592 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534721 true] [17592186305592 1111 #uuid "77dbf72a-adae-5231-b827-7a1763244fb7" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305593 1034 "{21}^{∘}" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305593 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534721 true] [17592186305593 1111 #uuid "a49f55ad-0b4a-59d1-9d05-998e90849253" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305594 1017 #edb/ref 17592186305595 13194139534721 true] [17592186305594 1089 "q-19040" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305594 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534721 true] [17592186305594 1100 "Given that $g\\cdot h=8$, find the angle between $g=⟨t,t,t-1⟩$ and $h=⟨4,-2,-1⟩.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139534721 true] [17592186305594 1113 #uuid "854d0f4a-8e08-5dc7-a816-ea56cbf65d2c" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305594 1145 "First, since $g\\cdot h=8$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =8 \\\\ t\\cdot 4+t\\cdot (-2)+(t-1)\\cdot (-1) & =8 \\\\ 4t-2t-t+1 & =8 \\\\ t+1 & =8 \\\\ t & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g & =⟨7,7,7-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,7,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $g$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{g\\cdot h}{|\\,g\\,||\\,h\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{g}_{x}{h}_{x}+{g}_{y}{h}_{y}+{g}_{z}{h}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{g}_{x}^{2}+{g}_{y}^{2}+{g}_{z}^{2}}\\sqrt{{h}_{x}^{2}+{h}_{y}^{2}+{h}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{134}\\cdot \\sqrt{21}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\,814}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2\\,814}})≈{81.33}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139534721 true] [17592186305595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305596 13194139534721 true] [17592186305595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305597 13194139534721 true] [17592186305595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186305598 13194139534721 true] [17592186305595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186